        "uric_acid": "Uric acid is formed when purines are broken down and is cleared mainly by the kidneys. High levels can contribute to gout or some kidney stones, although an elevated result does not always cause symptoms.",
        "urine_albumin": "Urine albumin measures leakage of a blood protein into urine, which can be an early sign of kidney damage. A concentration without urine creatinine is affected by how dilute the urine is.",
        "urine_appearance": "Urine appearance describes clarity or cloudiness. Cells, crystals, mucus or bacteria can change appearance; it is interpreted with the rest of urinalysis rather than used alone to identify disease.",
